    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1176-a1">

                <pb facs="1059" n="745" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg745"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Persia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>)</head>

                <opener>
                    <dateline>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-05T22:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 5, 1914, 10 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your undated. The Legation should maintain the attitude of strictest neutrality
                    in conformity with the proclamation issued by the President.</p>
                <p>You will instruct the Consul at Tabriz that he should use the greatest care and
                    discretion in extending protection to nationals other than American
                    citizens.</p>
                <p>Up to the present time the United States Government has not been requested to
                    take charge of German or Austrian interests in Persia.</p>
                <p rendition="#right">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                </p>
            </div>
